text:
November woods bare and still;
November days clear and bright;
Each noon burns up the mornings chill;
The mornings snow is gone by night.
Each day my steps grow slow grow light,
As through the woods | reverent creep.
Watching all things lie down to sleep
never knew before what beds
Fragrant to smell and soft to touch.
The forest sifts and shapes and spreads;
l never knew before how much
or human sound there IS in such
Low tones as through the forest sweep.
When all wild things lie down to sleep"
Each day ! find new coverlids
Tucked in, and more sweet eyes shut tight;
Sometimes the viewless mother bids
Her ferns kneel down full in my sight;
l hear their chorus of good nights;
And half smile, and half | weep,
Listening while they lie down to sleep"
November woods are bare and still;
November days are bright and good;
Lies noon burns up life's morning chill:
LIES night rests feet which long have stood
Some warm soft bed. in field wood,
The mother Will not fail to keep,
Where we can lay down to sleep"


-(Helen Hunt Jackson.

